{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790254121,"nonce":"QyxmhFISMxyOyrLc1yKcyoY44NQ=","message":"Explicit layouts landed in eff1d69 (bindgen) and b1dd788 (GPU).\n\n- Bindgen projects WebIDL unions declared as Rust enums whose variants carry one type: a record field of that type gets one setter per variant (GPUBindingResource becomes resourceSampler/resourceTexture/resourceTextureView/resourceBuffer/resourceBufferBinding on GpuBindGroupEntry). Variants are checked against the typedef's alternatives; a required union is not a constructor argument and the backend refuses it unset. Sequences of unions get add\u003cField\u003e\u003cVariant\u003e.\n- Keyword members (GPUBufferBindingLayout.type, GPUSamplerBindingLayout.type) are raw identifiers; plugin! exports them without r#.\n- Generated wrappers are now clippy-clean with -D warnings (enum codes evaluated at generation, derived Default, no let-and-return/unit bindings).\n- GPU: createBindGroupLayout / createPipelineLayout / createBindGroup / createComputePipeline from the IDL descriptors (GPUBindGroupLayoutEntry with buffer/sampler/texture/storageTexture/externalTexture layouts, GPUBufferBinding ranges, GPUProgrammableStage with constants, layout unset = auto), GpuPipeline.getBindGroupLayout, builder.layout(pipelineLayout), an open compute pass (computeBegin/SetPipeline/SetBindGroup/Dispatch/DispatchIndirect/End) and dynamic offsets in WebGPU's Uint32Array form for compute and render passes.\n- Fixture: explicitLayouts binds a dynamic storage window and a uniform range, overrides a constant and dispatches one group at two offsets. Passes on Apple M1 Pro/Metal, also with ASH_GC_STRESS=1 WLIFT_GC_STRESS=1; window_gpu still renders; wasm32-unknown-unknown checks.\n\nNot in this group: binding arrays (layout entry count), atomic storage-texture access and acceleration structures (wgpu extensions); external texture resources; render pipeline constants.","files":null}]}